# Every function in schema sys, by name and argument types. A test compares this list with the database catalog.
# Adding, removing, or changing the signature of a sys function without editing this file fails the build.
# A new line is a change to the bypass surface: say in the pull request why the function must exist.
#
# One function per line:  schema.name(argument types)  # what it is for

sys.current_space()                  # Reads the space id the transaction was opened for
sys.current_user_id()                # Reads the user id the transaction was opened for
sys.everyone()                       # The all-zero audience that means every member of the space
sys.claim_runs(text, integer)        # A worker leases runnable root runs across all spaces: queued, running with an expired lease, waiting with every approval answered, or waiting with a cancel request; returns ids only
sys.find_user_for_sign_in(text)      # Sign-in knows an email and no space; returns the user id only
sys.memberships_for_user()           # After sign-in, before a space is chosen: the spaces of the transaction's own user
sys.resolve_oauth_state(text)        # An OAuth callback has no tenant; maps the hash of its state to a space and user
sys.tool_sign_ins_running_out(timestamp with time zone, timestamp with time zone, timestamp with time zone, integer)  # Renewing tool server sign-ins ahead of time has no tenant: finds active sign-ins about to run out in every space, leaving out those tried and not renewed since a given moment and those renewed since another, one from each space before a second from any; returns ids only, never a secret id
sys.forget_tool_credentials(uuid)    # Removing a tool connection takes every sign-in to it: deletes the credential rows and their secrets of one connection, in the caller's own space only, across audiences; returns a count
sys.sandboxes_to_sweep(timestamp with time zone, timestamp with time zone, integer)  # Clearing up sandboxes has no tenant: finds, in every space, retired sandboxes that are due to be destroyed or may still be running, and rows left creating since before a given moment by an interrupted creation; returns space and sandbox ids only, never a secret id or a provider id
sys.purge_expired(integer)           # Deletes expired OAuth flows and destroyed, unreferenced sandboxes across spaces
sys.health()                         # Counts for the status page and the first-run check; no tenant data
sys.applied_migration()              # The status page compares the newest applied migration with the build's own; returns one migration id, no tenant data
